# Build context exclusions. Both images build from the repo root
# (docker-compose.prod.yml sets `context: .` for api and web), so this one
# file at the root covers both — there is no per-app context to scope.
#
# The reason this file exists: apps/api/Dockerfile does `COPY apps/api apps/api`
# and apps/web/Dockerfile does `COPY apps/web apps/web`. Without these rules
# that pulls apps/api/.env — the FASHN key, the JWT secret and the database
# password — into the builder layer. The final image is a clean second stage
# and never showed them, but `docker history` and any registry holding the
# builder cache did.
#
# Patterns are matched against the whole path from the context root, so a bare
# `node_modules` would only match the one at the root. Hence `**/`.

# --- secrets: the reason this file exists -----------------------------------
**/.env
**/.env.*

# --- dependencies and build output: reinstalled and rebuilt inside the image -
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/out
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- version control --------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- tests: they sit beside the code and must never ship --------------------
# apps/api/tsconfig.json already excludes these from the compiled output, but
# the runtime image now copies apps/api/src verbatim (prisma/seed.ts imports
# src/utils/crypto), so a rule that only governs tsc is no longer enough.
# Keeping them out of the context means no stage can copy them by accident.
**/*.test.ts
apps/api/src/test

# --- logs, test output, editor and OS noise ---------------------------------
**/*.log
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
.vscode
.idea

# --- local runtime state: dev file storage, never part of a build -----------
# apps/api/uploads is a named volume in production; anything here is local.
uploads
apps/api/uploads
**/tmp
backups

# --- host-only tooling ------------------------------------------------------
# Compose and nginx configure the stack from outside; copying them in would
# only invalidate layer cache when they change.
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile*
nginx
*.md
